  "reason": "The strongest completed result is RNA-only multiprofile PCA with avgpool (config_002, accuracy 0.5907), clearly better than single-profile PCA (config_001, 0.4849) and much better than image-only ResNet50 (config_010, 0.2079). This suggests multiprofile RNA representation is promising, but it is still unclear whether transformer aggregation would improve on avgpool. config_003 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the same RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA setup, so it isolates the effect of aggregation in the currently best direction. Under a limited budget, this is the most informative next step before adding image modality or fusion, because it tests an important design choice with minimal confounding changes."
